Cell["\<\
The note quotes \[CapitalDelta]L = 810 319 m (eq. 7) and \[CapitalDelta]t = \
2703.3 \[Micro]s (eq. 9). These are inconsistent: 810 319 m/c = 2702.93 \
\[Micro]s, and 2703.3 \[Micro]s corresponds to 810 429 m, the 2013 notebook \
value reproduced above. No combination of Table 2 antennas, offsets or \
MSL/ellipsoidal heights gives 810 319 m, so eq. 7 is most likely a \
transcription error. The spherical model is in any case only a consistency \
check. It overestimates the geocentric radii by ~10 km and is ~823 m too long.\
\>", "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Model 2: WGS84 ellipsoid (2014 note \[Section]3.2)", "Section"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Parameters, as used by both NOvA and MINOS (eqs. 10\[Dash]13). The note \
prints the radicand of eqs. 12\[Dash]13 divided by R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 ", and uses R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 " as the denominator of \[Epsilon]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 ". The first and second eccentricities are:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "a"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox["R", "a", "2"], "-", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["R", "b", "2"]}]], 
     SubscriptBox["R", "a"]]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "b"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox["R", "a", "2"], "-", 
       SubsuperscriptBox["R", "b", "2"]}]], 
     SubscriptBox["R", "b"]]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

