Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["FNAL height datum:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the Ash River heights are demonstrably ellipsoidal (\[Section]3.2). No \
NMEA record is given for FNAL. If 228 m is an MSL altitude, the ellipsoidal \
height is ~33 m lower (the geoid separation is not measured in the note; \
\[Minus]32.5 m at Ash River). See the sensitivity row above."
}], "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["FD horizontal offset:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the Ash River entries in Table 3 are TBD. The sensitivities above give the \
effect of the antenna-mast \[RightArrow] FD front-face horizontal vector once \
it is surveyed. Along the beam direction the effect is ~1 m of \
\[CapitalDelta]L per metre."
}], "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Endpoint:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the delay is ND cavern \[RightArrow] FD front face. Referencing the \
trigger to the spill at the NuMI target would add the target \[RightArrow] ND \
distance (~1 km, ~3.3 \[Micro]s) and the \[Pi]/K decay-point distribution \
along the 675 m decay pipe. That is presumably absorbed into the MIBS $74 \
reference and the 20 \[Micro]s sidebands."
}], "Item"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

