Cell[TextData[{
 "The Sagnac term is ",
 StyleBox["negative",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the FD rotates toward the westward-moving beam. The cable delay is not \
part of the flight time. It is a receiver calibration (the 1PPS is referenced \
to the antenna), common to all receivers on a mast, and must be compensated \
in the TDU configuration. It is the same order as the ND/FD offsets, so it \
should be checked."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["11. Errata in the 2014 note", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Eq. 7: \[CapitalDelta]L = 810 319 m is inconsistent with eq. 9 (2703.3 \
\[Micro]s \[DoubleLongRightArrow] 810 429 m). The value from the stated \
inputs is 810 429 m (\[Section]5).\
\>", "Item"],

Cell["Eq. 9: unit printed \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[Micro]t\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]; it should be \[Micro]s.", "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Eqs. 12\[Dash]13: the radicand is divided by R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 ", and \[Epsilon]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 " uses R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 ". They should be \[Epsilon]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 " = \[Sqrt](R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 "\.b2 \[Minus] R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 "\.b2)/R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 " and \[Epsilon]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 " = \[Sqrt](R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 "\.b2 \[Minus] R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 "\.b2)/R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 "."
}], "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Eq. 14: the numerator \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
means R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 ", and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sin \[Theta]\.b2\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] means \
sin\.b2\[Theta]."
}], "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Eq. 17: p",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "z"]]],
 " should be (R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "b"]]],
 "\.b2/R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "a"]]],
 "\.b2 R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "curv"]]],
 " + A) sin \[Theta]. The printed form also scales A. The effect is in \
\[Section]10.2."
}], "Item"],

Cell["\<\
Notation: \[Theta] is longitude in \[Section]3.1 but latitude in \
\[Section]3.2. The prime on \[CapitalDelta]p in eqs. 6 and 18 is typeset as a \
superscript \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]prime\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\
\>", "Item"],

Cell["\<\
Eq. 19: 809 606 m is the result of the 2013 inputs (300 m FNAL offset, no FD \
offset). The offsets specified in \[Section]3.1 and Table 2 (105 + 15 m, 12 + \
7.8 m) give the value in \[Section]7.2 (+10.1 m, +2.2 ticks).\
\>", "Item"],

Cell["\<\
\[Section]3.1 says the spherical model uses MSL altitude, but Table 2 heights \
are WGS84 ellipsoidal (\[Section]3.2 of this notebook).\
\>", "Item"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "R",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["", "E"]]],
 " is described as the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]mean equatorial radius\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. 6 378 137 m is the WGS84 equatorial radius."
}], "Item"],

Cell["\<\
Table 2: arc-minutes are marked with \[DoublePrime]. Ant-1 and Ant-2 have \
identical latitude/longitude and differ only in height (0.638 m).\
\>", "Item"],

Cell["\<\
Table 3: all Ash River offsets are TBD. The \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Fnal NDOS\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] row is labelled NDOS (a surface building) but \
annotated \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]105 + 15\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (the ND \
cavern), and its frame is unstated.\
\>", "Item"],

Cell["\<\
Placeholders: the DocDB number, and the antenna mount distance \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]XXX\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in \[Section]2.1. The \
References section is empty.\
\>", "Item"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

